          "The COVAX facility is an initiative of various international organisations, including the World Health Organisation (WHO) and Gavi, that aimed to ensure the equitable distribution of COVID-19 vaccines worldwide, particularly in developing countries (COVID-19 Cases, World, n.d.). In this regard, Bangladesh received millions and many more of vaccines through the COVAX facility, which was crucial in supporting its vaccination drive. Scholars highlight that Bangladesh pursued a pragmatic and diversified approach in its diplomacy by engaging various international actors simultaneously. These approaches included bilateral relations with India and China, negotiations with Russia over vaccine production cooperation, and engaging in multilateral approaches through the COVAX facility under the support of the WHO and other international organisations. Consequently, Dhaka was successful in vaccinating 569,825 individuals with the fourth dose as well. More than 90% of the population has gotten at least one dose of the COVID‐19 vaccine in Bangladesh.",
